    <p class="mh">Work with us</p><a class="mt" href="/careers"><b>Careers</b><small>Clinical education sales for RNs and LPNs</small></a>
    <p class="mh">Account</p><a class="mt" href="/#signup"><b>Join with a school code</b><small>Or request access</small></a><a class="mt" href="/#signin"><b>Sign in</b><small>Already have one</small></a>
   </div></details></nav></div></header><script>(function(){var d=document.querySelector(".mnav");if(!d)return;document.addEventListener("click",function(e){if(d.open&&!d.contains(e.target))d.open=false});document.addEventListener("keydown",function(e){if(e.key==="Escape"&&d.open){d.open=false;d.querySelector("summary").focus()}})})();</script><main><nav class="crumb w" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> › <span>NCLEX pass guarantee (fee reimbursement)</span></nav><section class="hero w hv"><div><h1>NCLEX Pass Guarantee: Your Registration Fee Back if You Qualify and Don't Pass</h1><p class="lead">This isn't a promise that you'll pass. Sign the agreement, meet every condition, and if you don't pass your first NCLEX-RN attempt after signing, Vexcura reimburses the registration fee you paid to Pearson VUE, up to $200. Students pay nothing for Vexcura. Their nursing school licenses it.</p><div class="cta"><a class="btn" href="/#progress">Read and sign in My Chart</a><a class="btn alt" href="#how">How it works</a></div></div><aside class="gq-box" aria-labelledby="gq-t"><p class="gq-k" id="gq-t">The terms, in plain language</p>
   <dl class="gq-dl"><div><dt>What's reimbursed</dt><dd>The NCLEX-RN registration fee you paid to Pearson VUE, <b>up to $200</b>. Nothing else.</dd></div><div><dt>Which attempt</dt><dd>Your <b>first NCLEX-RN attempt after you sign</b>. One reimbursement per person.</dd></div><div><dt>When</dt><dd>Only if your official result shows you <b>didn't pass</b> that attempt.</dd></div></dl>
   <p class="gq-k2">Every condition must be met before your NCLEX:</p>
   <ol class="gq-c"><li><b>Sign the agreement</b> in My Chart before the day of your NCLEX.</li><li><b>Usage Score of 98% or higher</b> on My Chart.</li><li><b>3 Qualifying Exams:</b> full adaptive exams in proctored test-day mode, 85+ questions, each ending in a Pass with a Clean integrity report.</li><li><b>No integrity flags</b> on any proctored practice exam after you sign.</li><li><b>Your NCLEX test date</b> entered in Vexcura beforehand.</li></ol>
   <p class="gq-k2">After your NCLEX:</p><p style="margin:0">Submit a claim from My Chart within <b>30 days</b> of your official result, then send your documents within <b>14 days</b> of our request.</p>
   <p class="gq-fine">You must also be 18 or older, live in the U.S., not have passed the NCLEX-RN before, and use your own account. <a href="#not-covered">What doesn't qualify</a> · <a href="#agreement">Full agreement</a></p></aside></section><div class="w"><style>
.gq-box{background:var(--surface);border:1px solid var(--line);border-top:5px solid var(--gold);border-radius:10px;padding:16px 18px 14px;box-shadow:0 1px 2px rgb(11 36 51/.06);font-size:15.5px;line-height:1.45}
.gq-k{margin:0 0 8px;font:700 12.5px/1.2 var(--fb);letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--gold)}
.gq-k2{margin:12px 0 6px;font-weight:700;font-size:15px}
.gq-dl{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr 1fr;gap:8px;margin:0}.gq-dl div{background:var(--bg);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:7px;padding:8px 10px}
.gq-dl dt{font-size:12.5px;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.04em;color:var(--muted)}.gq-dl dd{margin:2px 0 0;font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.35}
.gq-c{margin:0;padding:0;list-style:none;counter-reset:c;display:grid;gap:5px}.gq-c li{counter-increment:c;position:relative;padding-left:30px}
.gq-c li::before{content:counter(c);position:absolute;left:0;top:1px;width:21px;height:21px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--accent);color:var(--accent-ink);font:700 12.5px/21px var(--fb);text-align:center}
.gq-fine{margin:10px 0 0;font-size:13.5px;color:var(--muted)}
.gq-steps{list-style:none;counter-reset:s;margin:14px 0;padding:0;display:grid;gap:10px}.gq-steps li{counter-increment:s;position:relative;background:var(--surface);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:8px;padding:12px 14px 12px 56px}
.gq-steps li::before{content:counter(s);position:absolute;left:14px;top:12px;width:28px;height:28px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--navy);color:var(--flame);font:700 15px/28px var(--fb);text-align:center}.gq-steps b{display:block}
.gq-tot td{font-weight:700;background:var(--sunk)}.gq-pts{text-align:right;white-space:nowrap;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}
.gq-two{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(min(100%,300px),1fr));gap:14px;margin:14px 0}.gq-two>div{background:var(--surface);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:8px;padding:12px 16px}.gq-two h3{margin:4px 0 6px}.gq-two ul{margin:0;padding-left:20px}.gq-two li{margin:4px 0}
.gq .due .dn{height:auto}
.gq-note{background:var(--surface);border-left:4px solid var(--accent);padding:12px 16px;margin:18px 0;font-size:15.5px}
@media (max-width:860px){.gq-dl{grid-template-columns:1fr}}
@media (max-width:520px){.gq-box{padding:14px 14px 12px}.gq-steps li{padding-left:50px}.gq-steps li::before{left:11px}}</style><div class="gq">
   <p class="gq-note">Vexcura doesn't promise that you'll pass the NCLEX. The pass guarantee is a reimbursement of one registration fee, up to $200, for students who meet every condition below and don't pass their first attempt after signing.</p>
   <h2 id="how">How it works, step by step</h2>
   <ol class="gq-steps"><li><b>Get Vexcura through your nursing program</b>Vexcura is licensed to nursing schools, so students never pay. Join with the code from your instructor.</li><li><b>Read and sign the agreement before your NCLEX</b>Open My Chart, read the full agreement (version 2.1), check the three boxes, print your name and draw your signature. You have to sign before the day of your NCLEX. Your signed copy stays in your account.</li><li><b>Enter your NCLEX test date</b>Save your test date in Vexcura before you test.</li><li><b>Raise your Usage Score to 98% or higher</b>My Chart shows each part of the score, its target and your progress. The table below lists what earns points.</li><li><b>Pass 3 full exams in proctored test-day mode</b>Each one needs 85 or more questions, a Pass result and a Clean integrity report. Keep every proctored practice exam you take after signing Clean.</li><li><b>Take your NCLEX</b>If you pass, you're done and there's nothing to claim. The agreement ends when you pass.</li><li><b>If you don't pass, submit a claim within 30 days</b>Submit it from My Chart within 30 days of your official result. Within 14 days of our request, send your official result, your Pearson VUE receipt showing your name and the amount paid, and proof of identity.</li><li><b>Get a decision</b>Vexcura decides within 30 days of receiving all documents. If your claim is approved, Vexcura pays you by check or electronic transfer within 30 days. If it's denied, you're told why, and you can ask for a second review within 14 days.</li></ol>

   <h2 id="usage-score">The Usage Score: what earns points</h2>
   <p>The Usage Score on My Chart is the total of these seven parts, 100 points in all. You need <b>98% or higher</b> on or before the day of your NCLEX, so you can be short by no more than 2 points in total. You get partial points in proportion to your progress.</p>
   <div class="tw"><table><thead><tr><th>Part</th><th class="gq-pts">Points</th><th>Full points when</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Full exams in test-day mode</td><td class="gq-pts">20</td><td>3 Qualifying Exams</td></tr><tr><td>Question bank answered</td><td class="gq-pts">20</td><td>90% of the question bank answered at least once</td></tr><tr><td>Every NCLEX category practiced</td><td class="gq-pts">10</td><td>75% or more of each category's questions answered</td></tr><tr><td>Missed questions reviewed</td><td class="gq-pts">10</td><td>5 or fewer missed-question cards waiting, after at least 50 questions</td></tr><tr><td>Study days in the last 30</td><td class="gq-pts">15</td><td>20 study days</td></tr><tr><td>Study-plan orders completed</td><td class="gq-pts">10</td><td>10 completed orders</td></tr><tr><td>Clinical practice</td><td class="gq-pts">15</td><td>6 bedside cases, megacodes, or EHR simulation drills</td></tr><tr class="gq-tot"><td>Total</td><td class="gq-pts">100</td><td>98 or more needed</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
   <p>The targets that apply to you are the ones in the agreement version you sign. If the score on your device and Vexcura's records disagree, Vexcura's records count.</p>

   <h2 id="qualifying-exam">What counts as a Qualifying Exam</h2>
   <div class="split"><div class="st"><p>You need <b>3</b> Qualifying Exams before your NCLEX. Each one has to be:</p>
    <ul class="incl"><li>A full adaptive practice exam taken in your own account</li><li>Taken in proctored test-day mode, which produces an integrity report</li><li>At least 85 questions long</li><li>Ended with a <b>Pass</b> result</li><li>Given an integrity report that reads <b>Clean</b></li></ul>
    <p>Integrity reports read Clean, Minor flags or Irregular. Anything other than Clean is an integrity flag. A flag on any proctored practice exam you take after signing means you won't qualify. Exams with technical irregularities may be left out. <a href="/nclex-test-day-simulation">How test-day mode works</a> · <a href="/free-nclex-practice-exam">The full practice exam</a></p></div>
    <figure class="shot"><div class="dv dv-b"><div class="dv-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span><svg viewBox="0 0 12 14" width="9" height="11" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 6V4.2a3 3 0 0 1 6 0V6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6"/><rect x="1.5" y="6" width="9" height="7" rx="1.6" fill="currentColor"/></svg>nclexsim.com</span></div><div class="dv-v"><img src="/img/exam-results-1000.webp" srcset="/img/exam-results-1600.webp 1600w, /img/exam-results-1000.webp 1000w" sizes="(max-width: 760px) calc(100vw - 32px), 720px" width="1000" height="625" alt="Full practice exam results for a demo student: a 74% pass-likelihood estimate, labeled as an estimate, with ability by item" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></div></div><figcaption>A demo student's full-exam result: Pass, after 85 items. The pass likelihood is a practice estimate, not a prediction of the NCLEX.</figcaption></figure></div>
   <figure class="shot"><div class="dv dv-b"><div class="dv-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span><svg viewBox="0 0 12 14" width="9" height="11" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 6V4.2a3 3 0 0 1 6 0V6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6"/><rect x="1.5" y="6" width="9" height="7" rx="1.6" fill="currentColor"/></svg>nclexsim.com</span></div><div class="dv-v"><img src="/img/exam-q-1000.webp" srcset="/img/exam-q-1600.webp 1600w, /img/exam-q-1000.webp 1000w" sizes="(max-width: 760px) calc(100vw - 32px), 720px" width="1000" height="625" alt="The full adaptive NCLEX-RN practice exam in progress: item 5 with the five-hour timer, calculator and an answer selected" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></div></div><figcaption>Proctored test-day mode runs the same full adaptive exam: 85 to 150 items on a five-hour clock. Demo question.</figcaption></figure>

   <h2 id="claim">How to submit a claim</h2>
   <div class="due"><span><svg class="vxck" viewBox="0 0 100 100" role="img" aria-label="Current time"><circle class="cf" cx="50" cy="50" r="48"/><line x1="50" y1="6.5" x2="50" y2="13" transform="rotate(0 50 50)" class="mh"/><line x1="50" y1="7" x2="50" y2="9.6" transform="rotate(6 50 50)" class="mm"/><line x1="50" y1="7" x2="50" y2="9.6" transform="rotate(12 50 50)" class="mm"/><line x1="50" y1="7" x2="50" y2="9.6" transform="rotate(18 50 50)" class="mm"/><line x1="50" y1="7" x2="50" y2="9.6" transform="rotate(24 50 50)" class="mm"/><line x1="50" y1="6.5" x2="50" y2="13" transform="rotate(30 50 50)" class="mh"/><line x1="50" y1="7" x2="50" y2="9.6" transform="rotate(36 50 50)" class="mm"/><line x1="50" y1="7" x2="50" y2="9.6" transform="rotate(42 50 50)" class="mm"/><line x1="50" y1="7" x2="50" y2="9.6" transform="rotate(48 50 50)" class="mm"/><line x1="50" y1="7" x2="50" y2="9.6" transform="rotate(54 50 50)" class="mm"/><line x1="50" y1="6.5" x2="50" y2="13" transform="rotate(60 50 50)" class="mh"/><line x1="50" y1="7" x2="50" y2="9.6" transform="rotate(66 50 50)" class="mm"/><line x1="50" y1="7" x2="50" y2="9.6" transform="rotate(72 50 50)" class="mm"/><line x1="50" y1="7" x2="50" y2="9.6" transform="rotate(78 50 50)" class="mm"/><line x1="50" y1="7" x2="50" y2="9.6" transform="rotate(84 50 50)" class="mm"/><line x1="50" y1="6.5" x2="50" y2="13" transform="rotate(90 50 50)" class="mh"/><line x1="50" y1="7" x2="50" y2="9.6" transform="rotate(96 50 50)" class="mm"/><line x1="50" y1="7" x2="50" y2="9.6" transform="rotate(102 50 50)" class="mm"/><line x1="50" y1="7" x2="50" y2="9.6" transform="rotate(108 50 50)" class="mm"/><line x1="50" y1="7" x2="50" y2="9.6" transform="rotate(114 50 50)" class="mm"/><line x1="50" y1="6.5" x2="50" y2="13" transform="rotate(120 50 50)" class="mh"/><line x1="50" y1="7" x2="50" y2="9.6" transform="rotate(126 50 50)" class="mm"/><line x1="50" y1="7" x2="50" y2="9.6" transform="rotate(132 50 50)" class="mm"/><line x1="50" y1="7" x2="50" y2="9.6" transform="rotate(138 50 50)" class="mm"/><line x1="50" y1="7" x2="50" y2="9.6" transform="rotate(144 50 50)" class="mm"/><line x1="50" y1="6.5" x2="50" y2="13" transform="rotate(150 50 50)" class="mh"/><line x1="50" y1="7" x2="50" y2="9.6" transform="rotate(156 50 50)" class="mm"/><line x1="50" y1="7" x2="50" y2="9.6" transform="rotate(162 50 50)" class="mm"/><line x1="50" y1="7" x2="50" y2="9.6" transform="rotate(168 50 50)" class="mm"/><line x1="50" y1="7" x2="50" y2="9.6" transform="rotate(174 50 50)" class="mm"/><line x1="50" y1="6.5" x2="50" y2="13" transform="rotate(180 50 50)" class="mh"/><line x1="50" y1="7" x2="50" y2="9.6" transform="rotate(186 50 50)" class="mm"/><line x1="50" y1="7" x2="50" y2="9.6" transform="rotate(192 50 50)" class="mm"/><line x1="50" y1="7" x2="50" y2="9.6" transform="rotate(198 50 50)" class="mm"/><line x1="50" y1="7" x2="50" y2="9.6" transform="rotate(204 50 50)" class="mm"/><line x1="50" y1="6.5" x2="50" y2="13" transform="rotate(210 50 50)" class="mh"/><line x1="50" y1="7" x2="50" y2="9.6" transform="rotate(216 50 50)" class="mm"/><line x1="50" y1="7" x2="50" y2="9.6" transform="rotate(222 50 50)" class="mm"/><line x1="50" y1="7" x2="50" y2="9.6" transform="rotate(228 50 50)" class="mm"/><line x1="50" y1="7" x2="50" y2="9.6" transform="rotate(234 50 50)" class="mm"/><line x1="50" y1="6.5" x2="50" y2="13" transform="rotate(240 50 50)" class="mh"/><line x1="50" y1="7" x2="50" y2="9.6" transform="rotate(246 50 50)" class="mm"/><line x1="50" y1="7" x2="50" y2="9.6" transform="rotate(252 50 50)" class="mm"/><line x1="50" y1="7" x2="50" y2="9.6" transform="rotate(258 50 50)" class="mm"/><line x1="50" y1="7" x2="50" y2="9.6" transform="rotate(264 50 50)" class="mm"/><line x1="50" y1="6.5" x2="50" y2="13" transform="rotate(270 50 50)" class="mh"/><line x1="50" y1="7" x2="50" y2="9.6" transform="rotate(276 50 50)" class="mm"/><line x1="50" y1="7" x2="50" y2="9.6" transform="rotate(282 50 50)" class="mm"/><line x1="50" y1="7" x2="50" y2="9.6" transform="rotate(288 50 50)" class="mm"/><line x1="50" y1="7" x2="50" y2="9.6" transform="rotate(294 50 50)" class="mm"/><line x1="50" y1="6.5" x2="50" y2="13" transform="rotate(300 50 50)" class="mh"/><line x1="50" y1="7" x2="50" y2="9.6" transform="rotate(306 50 50)" class="mm"/><line x1="50" y1="7" x2="50" y2="9.6" transform="rotate(312 50 50)" class="mm"/><line x1="50" y1="7" x2="50" y2="9.6" transform="rotate(318 50 50)" class="mm"/><line x1="50" y1="7" x2="50" y2="9.6" transform="rotate(324 50 50)" class="mm"/><line x1="50" y1="6.5" x2="50" y2="13" transform="rotate(330 50 50)" class="mh"/><line x1="50" y1="7" x2="50" y2="9.6" transform="rotate(336 50 50)" class="mm"/><line x1="50" y1="7" x2="50" y2="9.6" transform="rotate(342 50 50)" class="mm"/><line x1="50" y1="7" x2="50" y2="9.6" transform="rotate(348 50 50)" class="mm"/><line x1="50" y1="7" x2="50" y2="9.6" transform="rotate(354 50 50)" class="mm"/><g class="ch"><line x1="50" y1="56" x2="50" y2="27"/></g><g class="cm"><line x1="50" y1="57" x2="50" y2="12"/></g><g class="cs"><line x1="50" y1="62" x2="50" y2="9"/><circle cx="50" cy="50" r="2.8"/></g><circle class="cc" cx="50" cy="50" r="1.3"/></svg></span><div><p class="dk">Claim deadline</p><p class="dn">30 days<span> from your official result</span></p><p>Claims are submitted in My Chart. Once you've signed, a <b>Submit a claim</b> button appears there.</p></div></div>
   <ol><li>In My Chart, choose <b>Submit a claim</b>. Enter the date you took the NCLEX-RN and the registration fee you paid, then confirm that you took it on that date, didn't pass, did all of your Vexcura practice yourself, and that everything you entered is true.</li>
    <li>Within <b>14 days</b> of our request, send: a complete copy of your official result, your Pearson VUE registration receipt showing your name and the amount paid, proof of identity, and anything else we reasonably ask for to verify the claim. The name on every document has to match the name you printed when you signed.</li>
    <li>Vexcura reviews your exam history, integrity reports and activity, then decides within <b>30 days</b> of receiving all your documents. The decision goes to the email on your account.</li>
    <li>If your claim is approved, you're paid within <b>30 days</b>. If it's denied, you're told why, and you can ask in writing for a second review within <b>14 days</b>.</li></ol>
   <p>You can have only one claim open at a time, and only one reimbursement is ever paid per person.</p>

   <h2 id="not-covered">What doesn't qualify</h2>
   <div class="gq-two"><div><h3>Not covered</h3><ul><li>Any NCLEX attempt after the first one you take after signing</li><li>The NCLEX-PN</li><li>Licensure, application, background-check and fingerprinting fees</li><li>Travel, lodging, lost wages and other expenses</li><li>Other study materials or courses</li><li>An attempt you didn't complete or attend, or that you rescheduled or cancelled</li><li>An attempt whose results were withheld, cancelled or invalidated</li></ul></div>
    <div><h3>No reimbursement if</h3><ul><li>You signed on or after the day of your NCLEX</li><li>Any condition above isn't met: Usage Score, 3 Qualifying Exams, no integrity flags, or test date entered</li><li>Your claim is late, incomplete or not backed by the required documents</li><li>You're under 18, live outside the U.S., have already passed the NCLEX-RN, or already received a reimbursement</li><li>You're an owner, employee or contractor of Vexcura, or live in their household</li><li>Someone else used your account or did any of your practice, you used automated tools, or you changed any record. This is a material breach, and any payment has to be repaid.</li><li>You withdrew before your NCLEX, or 12 months passed after signing with no NCLEX attempt</li></ul></div></div>

   <h2 id="agreement">The full agreement</h2>
   <p>The program is governed by the <b>Vexcura NCLEX-RN Fee Reimbursement Agreement, version 2.1</b>. Students read the full agreement in My Chart before signing, and the signature section only unlocks once you scroll to the end. Your signed copy, with the date, time and a fingerprint of the exact text, stays in your account, where you can view, print or save it as a PDF. You can withdraw at any time from My Chart. This page is a summary. No ad or page changes the agreement, and if they ever differ, the agreement controls.</p>
   <div class="cta"><a class="btn" href="/#progress">Read the agreement in My Chart</a><a class="btn alt" href="/#signin">Sign in</a></div>

   <h2 id="schools">For nursing schools</h2>
   <p>Faculty can tell students about the fee reimbursement as part of NCLEX readiness. It rewards the habits programs already ask for: full practice exams under test-day conditions, missed-question review and steady study. The agreement is between Vexcura and each student. Your program isn't a party to it and doesn't handle claims. <a href="/for-nursing-schools">Vexcura for nursing schools</a></p>

   <h2 id="faq">Questions about the NCLEX pass guarantee (fee reimbursement)</h2><details class="faq"><summary>Does Vexcura guarantee I'll pass the NCLEX?</summary><p>No. Vexcura doesn't promise or predict that anyone will pass. What we call the pass guarantee is a fee reimbursement: if you sign the agreement, meet every condition and don't pass your first NCLEX-RN attempt after signing, Vexcura reimburses the registration fee you paid to Pearson VUE, up to $200.</p></details><details class="faq"><summary>Is this an NCLEX money-back guarantee?</summary><p>Only for the NCLEX registration fee, and only if you qualify. Students don't pay Vexcura anything, because nursing schools license it. So the money you can get back is the NCLEX-RN registration fee you paid to Pearson VUE, up to $200, and only if you meet every condition and don't pass your first attempt after signing.</p></details><details class="faq"><summary>How much is reimbursed, and how is it paid?</summary><p>The registration fee you personally paid to Pearson VUE for that attempt, up to $200. It's paid to you only, by check or electronic transfer, within 30 days after your claim is approved. You're responsible for any taxes that apply.</p></details><details class="faq"><summary>What is the Usage Score?</summary><p>A score from 0 to 100 on My Chart that shows how fully you've used Vexcura: full exams, how much of the question bank you've answered, every NCLEX category, missed-question review, study days, study-plan orders and clinical practice. You need 98% or higher, so you can be short by no more than 2 points in total. If your device and Vexcura's records disagree, Vexcura's records count.</p></details><details class="faq"><summary>What counts as a Qualifying Exam?</summary><p>A full adaptive practice exam taken in your own account in proctored test-day mode. It has to have at least 85 questions, end with a Pass result and have an integrity report that reads Clean. You need 3 of them before your NCLEX.</p></details><details class="faq"><summary>Do practice exams I took before signing count?</summary><p>Yes. Qualifying Exams count if they were completed before your NCLEX, even if you took them before you signed. The no-integrity-flags condition applies to proctored practice exams taken after you sign.</p></details><details class="faq"><summary>What if a proctored practice exam gets a Minor flags or Irregular report?</summary><p>Any report other than Clean is an integrity flag. One flag on a proctored practice exam taken after you sign means that condition isn't met, so you won't qualify for reimbursement under that agreement.</p></details><details class="faq"><summary>When do I have to sign?</summary><p>Before the day of your NCLEX, in My Chart. Reimbursement only covers the first NCLEX-RN attempt you take after signing. If no attempt happens within 12 months of signing, the agreement ends.</p></details><details class="faq"><summary>How long do I have to file a claim?</summary><p>You have 30 days from the date of your official result to submit your claim in My Chart. After we ask for documents, you have 14 days to send them. Late or incomplete claims are denied.</p></details><details class="faq"><summary>Can I read the full agreement before I sign?</summary><p>Yes. The full agreement (version 2.1) is in My Chart, and the signature section only unlocks once you scroll to the end. After you sign, you can view, print or save your signed copy any time, and you can withdraw from My Chart whenever you want. If this page and the agreement ever differ, the agreement controls.</p></details><details class="faq"><summary>Does it cover the NCLEX-PN or a retake?</summary><p>No. It covers only the NCLEX-RN registration fee for the first attempt after you sign. Later attempts, the NCLEX-PN, and licensure, application, background-check and fingerprinting fees aren't covered.</p></details><details class="faq"><summary>How do I get Vexcura?</summary><p>Through your nursing program. Vexcura is licensed to nursing schools and facilities, and it's free for their students and instructors. If your program doesn't use Vexcura yet, send your faculty to nclexsim.com/for-nursing-schools.</p></details>
   <p class="src" style="color:var(--muted);font-size:14.5px">Vexcura does not promise or guarantee that you will pass the NCLEX. Practice results, readiness estimates and pass-likelihood figures are study aids and don't predict your NCLEX result. Terms are summarized from agreement version 2.1, current as of November 2026. NCLEX® and NCLEX-RN® are registered trademarks of the National Council of State Boards of Nursing, Inc.</p></div><h2>Related</h2><ul class="rel"><li><a href="/free-nclex-practice-exam">Full adaptive NCLEX-RN practice exam</a></li><li><a href="/nclex-test-day-simulation">Proctored test-day rehearsal</a></li><li><a href="/nclex-practice-questions">Free NCLEX practice questions by category</a></li><li><a href="/for-nursing-schools">Vexcura for nursing schools</a></li><li><a href="/nclex-study-guides">Free NCLEX study guides (PDF)</a></li></ul></div><section class="band vxs-band"><div class="vxs-bg" data-vxs-i="0" aria-hidden="true"></div><div class="vxs-sh" aria-hidden="true"></div><div class="w"><h2>Students get Vexcura through their nursing program</h2><p>Vexcura is licensed to nursing schools and facilities, and it's free for their students and instructors. Join with your school code, or send your faculty the page for programs.</p><div class="cta"><a class="btn" href="/#signup">Join with a school code</a><a class="btn alt" href="/for-nursing-schools">For nursing schools</a></div></div></section></main><footer class="foot"><div class="w"><div class="cols">
